{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>What profit.</b> What benefit? For vengeance indeed aims at one of two things: either to requite evildoers — yet in this case, if we kill our brother, we requite evil upon ourselves as well, for our hearts will ache over his death and over our cruelty toward him. Or to frighten the rest, so that they hear and fear to harm us — yet this kind of benefit too we will not attain, for we will conceal his death." "<b>And we shall conceal his blood.</b> For our honor and for fear of our father."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:42.464815579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}